# fw_env.config — libubootenv (fw_printenv / fw_setenv) for Zion Kria boards
#
# The Zion U-Boot (xilinx_zynqmp_kria) stores its environment as a binary
# env image (CONFIG_ENV_SIZE=0x20000) in the FAT boot partition (p1):
#   CONFIG_ENV_FAT_DEVICE_AND_PART=":auto" -> uboot.env on the first FAT
# libubootenv 0.3.5+ supports regular files (DEVICE_FILE), so we point at
# the mounted boot partition copy. The redundant copy is listed second.
#
# NOTE: slot switching does NOT depend on the U-Boot env — boot.cmd.zion
# reads the slot state from marker files on /boot. These entries only
# enable the optional fw_setenv bookkeeping.

/boot/uboot.env       0x0     0x20000
/boot/uboot-redund.env 0x0    0x20000